7(a) CALCULATE THE SUM OF ARRAY ELEMENTS

AIM:

To calculate the sum of elements in an array using methods and user input.

ALGORITHM / PROCEDURE:

Start the program execution by creating the main method.
Prompt the user to enter the number of elements in the array.
Declare and initialize an integer array of the given size.
Read the elements of the array using a loop and store them in the array.
Pass the array to a method named calculateSum(int[] arr).
Inside the calculateSum method, initialize sum = 0 and add each array element to the sum.
Return the final sum to the main method and display the result.

PROGRAM:

import java.util.Scanner;

public class SumArray {

public static int calculateSum(int[] arr) {
    int sum = 0;

    for (int num : arr) {
        sum += num;
    }

    return sum;
}

public static void main(String[] args) {
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

    System.out.print("Enter number of elements: ");
    int n = sc.nextInt();

    int[] array = new int[n];

    System.out.println("Enter the elements:");

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        array[i] = sc.nextInt();
    }

    int total = calculateSum(array);

    System.out.println("Sum of array elements: " + total);
}

}

OUTPUT:

Enter number of elements: 5
Enter the elements:
1 2 3 4 5
Sum of array elements: 15

RESULT:

The program works correctly and computes the sum of array elements using a method.

