7(b) SELECTION SORT

AIM:

To sort an array using Selection Sort method in Java.

ALGORITHM / PROCEDURE:

Start the program by creating the main method.
Prompt the user to enter the number of elements and initialize an integer array.
Read all elements of the array from the user.
Call the method selectionSort(int[] arr) to sort the array in ascending order.
Inside the selectionSort method, iterate through the array and assume the current index as the minimum index.
Compare the current element with the remaining unsorted elements and find the minimum element.
Swap the minimum element with the current element.
Repeat the process until the entire array is sorted and display the sorted array.

PROGRAM:

import java.util.Scanner;

public class SelectionSort {

public static void selectionSort(int[] arr) {

    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; i++) {

        int minIndex = i;

        for (int j = i + 1; j < arr.length; j++) {

            if (arr[j] < arr[minIndex]) {
                minIndex = j;
            }
        }

        int temp = arr[minIndex];
        arr[minIndex] = arr[i];
        arr[i] = temp;
    }
}

public static void main(String[] args) {

    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

    System.out.print("Enter number of elements: ");
    int n = sc.nextInt();

    int[] array = new int[n];

    System.out.println("Enter the elements:");

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        array[i] = sc.nextInt();
    }

    selectionSort(array);

    System.out.println("Sorted array:");

    for (int num : array) {
        System.out.print(num + " ");
    }
}

}

OUTPUT:

Enter number of elements: 5
Enter the elements:
5 3 8 1 2
Sorted array: 1 2 3 5 8

RESULT:

The program sorts the array using selection sort method correctly.

