8(a) REVERSE A STRING

AIM:

To reverse a string using method and user input in Java.

ALGORITHM / PROCEDURE:

Start the program execution by defining the main method.
Prompt the user to enter a string using the Scanner class.
Pass the string to a separate method named reverse(String str).
Inside the reverse method, initialize an empty string variable named reversed.
Traverse the input string from the last character to the first character using a loop.
Append each character to the reversed string.
Return the reversed string to the main method.
Display the reversed string.

PROGRAM:

import java.util.Scanner;

public class ReverseString {

public static String reverse(String str) {

    String reversed = "";

    for (int i = str.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        reversed += str.charAt(i);
    }

    return reversed;
}

public static void main(String[] args) {

    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

    System.out.print("Enter a string: ");
    String input = sc.nextLine();

    String output = reverse(input);

    System.out.println("Reversed String: " + output);
}

}

OUTPUT:

Enter a string: Hello
Reversed String: olleH

RESULT:

The program successfully reverses a string using a method.

